{% set local_problem %}
<p>Alabama's humidity is brutal on exposed wood. When gutters clog or leak, water runs behind them and soaks into fascia boards. In Madison's climate, that moisture doesn't dry out — it sits there, creating perfect conditions for rot and mold.</p>

<p>We see it constantly: homeowners call for new gutters, but when we inspect their homes, we find fascia that's soft, water-stained, or visibly rotting. Installing new gutters on damaged wood is pointless — they won't stay attached, and the underlying damage will only get worse.</p>

<p>Many Madison homes built in the last 10-20 years used lower-quality wood or composite materials for fascia. Combined with builder-grade gutters that leak at seams, these homes are especially prone to fascia damage. The good news is that repair is straightforward when caught early.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>We start with a thorough inspection, checking fascia (and soffit if needed) for water damage, soft spots, and rot. We'll show you exactly what we find and explain what needs repair.</p>

<p>For damaged sections, we carefully remove existing gutters, cut out the rotted wood, and install new fascia boards. We use quality primed lumber or composite materials designed for exterior exposure. Everything is sealed and prepared for new gutter installation.</p>

<p>Then we install your new gutters on the fresh fascia — properly attached, properly sloped, and designed to prevent the overflow that caused the problem in the first place. You get a complete solution with one contractor and one warranty.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set why_us %}
<p>We've been repairing fascia and installing gutters in Madison for over 20 years. We understand that these two jobs go hand-in-hand — you can't have reliable gutters without solid fascia, and you can't protect fascia without properly functioning gutters.</p>

<p>Our crews handle both carpentry and gutter installation, which means better coordination, cleaner work, and a single point of accountability. When we're done, your home is fully protected from roof edge to foundation.</p>
{% endset %}
